course: dictionary
lesson: 14965
title: A new place: relocation
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Relocation is a long word, but you can break it into parts. It comes from relocate, which means to move to a new place. The ending -ion turns it into a noun, so relocation is the act of moving.
explain: «The family's relocation to Manchester took three days.» The clues are family, Manchester and three days. Those words show people packing up and moving home, so relocation means moving to a new place to live.
explain: The word can also be about work, animals and things. «The company paid for Mum's relocation to the new office.» Here it means moving to a new place for work. Read the whole sentence, and check your meaning fits.
fact: Relocation is a noun. The verb is relocate, and the plural is relocations.
fact: «Relocation» means moving to a new place to live or work.
fact: «Relocation» can also mean moving animals, things or buildings to a new place.
fact: «Relocation costs» are the costs of moving home or work, such as the van and the trip.
fact: «A relocation package» is the help and money a company gives a worker who has to move.
exercise: «The family's relocation to Manchester took three days.» What is a relocation? | *Moving to a new place to live | A type of cake | A visit for one afternoon | Buying a new car
exercise: Wildlife experts plan the relocation of otters to a quieter river. What does relocation mean here? | Counting the fish | Painting the river blue | *Moving the otters to a new place | Feeding the otters every day
exercise: What is a «relocation package»? | A bag for carrying school books | A holiday for the whole family | A parcel sent by post | *Help and money a company gives to cover a move
test: «The museum's relocation took two weeks, as every painting went to a new building.» What is the relocation? | A closing down | *A move to a new place | A guided tour | A new painting
test: «Relocation to a new job often means making new friends.» What does relocation mean in this sentence? | *Moving to a new place for work | Losing a job | Making a new friend | Staying in the same office
exam: Which word means nearly the same as relocation? | *Moving | Sleeping | Waiting | Staying
